Assign Meeting Rooms
====================

Write a function:

    def assign_meeting_rooms(meetings: list[list[int]]) -> tuple[int, dict]

meetings is a list of [start, end] intervals. Assign every meeting to a room
so that no two meetings in the same room overlap; a meeting can follow
another in the same room if it starts at or after the previous one ends.
Sort the meetings by start time, then place each one in the LOWEST-numbered
room that is free (first-fit), opening a new room only when none is free.
Return a tuple (rooms_needed, rooms) where rooms maps each room number
(0, 1, ...) to the list of meetings assigned to it.

Examples:
    assign_meeting_rooms([[9, 10], [9, 12], [11, 13]]) -> (2, {0: [[9, 10], [11, 13]], 1: [[9, 12]]})
    assign_meeting_rooms([[8, 9], [9, 10], [10, 11]]) -> (1, {0: [[8, 9], [9, 10], [10, 11]]})
    assign_meeting_rooms([[10, 20], [15, 25], [20, 30], [5, 10]]) -> (2, {0: [[5, 10], [10, 20], [20, 30]], 1: [[15, 25]]})
    assign_meeting_rooms([]) -> (0, {})
